= Hypertext Transfer Protocol — Simple =

The Hypertext Transfer Protocol (HTTP) is a stateless application-layer protocol with extensible semantics for interacting with networked resources.

HTTP defines request methods, response status codes, fields, representation metadata, caching semantics, and related interaction rules. It is central to the Web but is also used by APIs and other network services.

'''Important boundaries:'''
* HTTP ≠ HTML
* HTTP ≠ World Wide Web

